    "body": "## Description\n\nCreate a `docs/architecture.md` placeholder that describes the planned high-level components of HoneyBee Browser.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `docs/architecture.md`.\n2. Add a section for each of these planned modules:\n   - **Browser shell (UI)** - window, tabs, URL bar.\n   - **Networking** - HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2.\n   - **HTML parser** - tokenizer and tree builder.\n   - **CSS engine** - cascade and selectors.\n   - **Layout** - box model, block and inline flow.\n   - **JavaScript** - planned engine and DOM bindings.\n   - **Inter-process communication (IPC)** - once the multi-process model is introduced.\n3. For each module, write 2-3 sentences explaining its role.\n4. End the file with a \"Further Reading\" section linking to relevant Wikipedia articles.\n5. Commit with `docs: add architecture overview`.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Writing technical documentation.\n- Understanding browser architecture at a high level.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [How Browsers Work (Web.dev)](https://web.dev/articles/howbrowserswork)\n- [MDN: How browsers work](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Performance/How_browsers_work)\n",
